WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.272 --> 00:00:03.535
Welcome to the updated Fire Toolshed hazardous
materials workflow.

2
00:00:03.499 --> 00:00:06.777
We will follow the live user guides from the
owner's safety data sheets through

3
00:00:06.777 --> 00:00:10.220
classification, owner quantities, maximum
allowable quantity review, and room notes

4
00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:10.635
for Revit.

5
00:00:10.635 --> 00:00:13.510
These are actual screenshots captured while
using the published app.

6
00:00:13.510 --> 00:00:17.149
The products, quantities, and returned analysis
are clearly labeled training

7
00:00:17.149 --> 00:00:17.580
examples.

8
00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:20.732
They demonstrate the controls, not a completed
engineering assessment.

9
00:00:21.599 --> 00:00:23.815
Step one: start in the bulk workspace.

10
00:00:23.778 --> 00:00:25.754
Expand Project and code basis.

11
00:00:25.754 --> 00:00:29.824
Enter the project name, jurisdiction, reviewer,
assessment basis, and adopted code

12
00:00:29.824 --> 00:00:30.221
edition.

13
00:00:30.221 --> 00:00:33.764
Confirm amendments and project requirements
before exporting an AI batch.

14
00:00:33.764 --> 00:00:37.435
Use one workspace for the project, adding later
deliveries to that same workspace.

15
00:00:37.435 --> 00:00:40.986
The edition shown here is a training
placeholder; a real assessment needs the actual

16
00:00:40.986 --> 00:00:41.747
governing edition.

17
00:00:42.597 --> 00:00:45.887
Name the delivery so you can recognize its
building, date, or sender.

18
00:00:45.851 --> 00:00:48.830
Select PDFs or ZIP archives and choose the
owner's files.

19
00:00:48.830 --> 00:00:50.589
Combined PDFs are allowed.

20
00:00:50.589 --> 00:00:52.563
Keep the tab open while the app reads them.

21
00:00:52.563 --> 00:00:56.878
The limits are one hundred mebibytes per PDF and
one gibibyte of expanded PDF data

22
00:00:56.878 --> 00:00:57.299
per ZIP.

23
00:00:57.299 --> 00:00:58.858
Split larger deliveries.

24
00:00:58.858 --> 00:01:02.141
Pause after current page lets you stop reading
without losing the registered

25
00:01:02.141 --> 00:01:02.616
identities.

26
00:01:03.458 --> 00:01:05.517
Step two: account for the documents.

27
00:01:05.481 --> 00:01:09.427
Export the receipt log and reconcile every
delivered file as registered, duplicate,

28
00:01:09.427 --> 00:01:10.521
or explicitly excluded.

29
00:01:10.521 --> 00:01:12.850
Then use Confirm documents and page ranges.

30
00:01:12.850 --> 00:01:15.180
Here, two PDFs still need range review.

31
00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:19.155
A filename is not a verified product identity,
and one PDF may contain several

32
00:01:19.155 --> 00:01:19.614
products.

33
00:01:19.614 --> 00:01:23.710
Use Find a source and the Show filter to focus
on failed files, unreadable pages, or

34
00:01:23.710 --> 00:01:24.636
unconfirmed ranges.

35
00:01:25.493 --> 00:01:28.237
Select Review source, then Open original PDF.

36
00:01:28.201 --> 00:01:32.130
Check product name, manufacturer, product
number, and revision against the actual

37
00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:32.567
document.

38
00:01:32.567 --> 00:01:34.211
Set the start and end pages.

39
00:01:34.211 --> 00:01:37.458
For a combined PDF, add one range for each
safety data sheet.

40
00:01:37.458 --> 00:01:39.433
Assign every page exactly once.

41
00:01:39.433 --> 00:01:42.074
Mark cover pages Not an SDS and explain why.

42
00:01:42.074 --> 00:01:44.378
Confirm page coverage only after checking it.

43
00:01:44.378 --> 00:01:48.128
Keep the permanent material IDs, including when
linking an existing assessment.

44
00:01:48.947 --> 00:01:52.289
Read or correct extracted text is the recovery
path for poor documents.

45
00:01:52.253 --> 00:01:56.437
The app extracts existing PDF text; it does not
perform optical character recognition

46
00:01:56.437 --> 00:01:56.782
itself.

47
00:01:56.782 --> 00:02:00.790
Use your chosen OCR tool when necessary, paste
the readable text, compare it with the

48
00:02:00.790 --> 00:02:03.242
original page, check the verification box, and
save.

49
00:02:03.242 --> 00:02:06.816
Straightforward single-sheet documents can be
reviewed in groups using Review next

50
00:02:06.816 --> 00:02:08.342
twenty-five single-SDS suggestions.

51
00:02:08.342 --> 00:02:11.313
Combined or uncertain files still need
individual attention.

52
00:02:12.159 --> 00:02:14.643
Step three: classify the confirmed products.

53
00:02:14.607 --> 00:02:18.449
In Analyze and review products, click Select
next twenty-five without results, or

54
00:02:18.449 --> 00:02:19.777
select individual materials.

55
00:02:19.777 --> 00:02:22.436
Twenty-five is recommended; fifty is the
maximum.

56
00:02:22.436 --> 00:02:24.167
Our small example selects two.

57
00:02:24.167 --> 00:02:26.195
Click Export selected AI batch.

58
00:02:26.195 --> 00:02:31.071
The ZIP contains original PDFs, extracted text,
stable IDs, the project basis, and

59
00:02:31.071 --> 00:02:32.498
AI-INSTRUCTIONS dot txt.

60
00:02:32.498 --> 00:02:35.598
The app does not run a hosted AI model or send
this package for you.

61
00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:40.060
Give that ZIP to your approved AI, together with
authorized governing code text and

62
00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:40.537
amendments.

63
00:02:40.501 --> 00:02:42.919
Tell it to follow AI-INSTRUCTIONS dot txt.

64
00:02:42.919 --> 00:02:46.176
Those instructions require reading the complete
sheets, evaluating physical and

65
00:02:46.176 --> 00:02:49.681
health hazards, and returning the same JSON
structure with unchanged IDs and document

66
00:02:49.681 --> 00:02:50.218
fingerprints.

67
00:02:50.218 --> 00:02:53.188
Safety labels alone do not establish code
classifications.

68
00:02:53.188 --> 00:02:55.232
Missing evidence becomes an open question.

69
00:02:55.232 --> 00:02:58.567
Quantities remain unknown, and reviewer
validation stays with a person.

70
00:02:59.395 --> 00:03:02.208
Bring the returned JSON back through Preview AI
results.

71
00:03:02.172 --> 00:03:06.009
Check the returned count, missing batch records,
and identity and source checks.

72
00:03:06.009 --> 00:03:09.083
Fix import errors before choosing Merge checked
analysis results.

73
00:03:09.083 --> 00:03:12.479
This demonstration response deliberately leaves
the technical classification

74
00:03:12.479 --> 00:03:12.971
unresolved.

75
00:03:12.971 --> 00:03:16.577
A successful merge means the records were
accepted; it does not mean the hazards are

76
00:03:16.577 --> 00:03:17.006
validated.

77
00:03:17.006 --> 00:03:19.102
Existing owner inventory is preserved.

78
00:03:19.102 --> 00:03:22.627
Use Analysis batch reconciliation to find
partial or missing responses before

79
00:03:22.627 --> 00:03:23.726
starting the next batch.

80
00:03:24.578 --> 00:03:28.491
Open Review product to inspect the identity,
linked source range, proposed hazards,

81
00:03:28.491 --> 00:03:30.188
evidence, and outstanding questions.

82
00:03:30.152 --> 00:03:34.222
Check mixture composition, concentration,
physical state, and conditions of use.

83
00:03:34.222 --> 00:03:37.921
Do not assume a pure component classification
automatically applies to the mixture.

84
00:03:37.921 --> 00:03:41.368
Repeat the batch process until every confirmed
product has results or a clearly

85
00:03:41.368 --> 00:03:42.371
recorded open question.

86
00:03:42.371 --> 00:03:45.942
For a real project, resolve the classification
questions before treating this stage

87
00:03:45.942 --> 00:03:46.458
as finished.

88
00:03:47.323 --> 00:03:50.292
Step four: get quantities from the person who
knows the site.

89
00:03:50.256 --> 00:03:51.616
Download owner workbook.

90
00:03:51.616 --> 00:03:54.604
Product identities and permanent IDs are already
filled in.

91
00:03:54.604 --> 00:03:56.196
Send that workbook to the owner.

92
00:03:56.196 --> 00:03:59.358
Keep Material IDs and existing Inventory IDs
unchanged.

93
00:03:59.358 --> 00:04:01.392
Use one row per material and location.

94
00:04:01.392 --> 00:04:05.094
For another location, copy the row, keep the
Material ID, and clear the Inventory ID

95
00:04:05.094 --> 00:04:07.298
so the app can create a separate inventory
record.

96
00:04:08.149 --> 00:04:12.165
Ask the owner to confirm on-site status,
building, room, process, and maximum

97
00:04:12.165 --> 00:04:14.512
storage, closed-use, and open-use quantities.

98
00:04:14.476 --> 00:04:18.402
Use plain numbers with a supported unit, not
formulas or descriptions such as two

99
00:04:18.402 --> 00:04:18.693
drums.

100
00:04:18.693 --> 00:04:21.664
Leave unknown values blank; zero means confirmed
absent.

101
00:04:21.664 --> 00:04:25.145
The optional owner total is independent because
storage and use can overlap.

102
00:04:25.145 --> 00:04:27.440
Include who confirmed the information and when.

103
00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:29.389
Do not guess control-area boundaries.

104
00:04:29.389 --> 00:04:32.202
Record exclusions explicitly rather than
deleting rows.

105
00:04:33.055 --> 00:04:35.305
Select Load returned Excel or CSV.

106
00:04:35.269 --> 00:04:38.638
Choose the worksheet, check the column mapping,
then build the inventory preview.

107
00:04:38.638 --> 00:04:43.149
Review additions, updates, locations, unit
conversions, and unresolved information.

108
00:04:43.149 --> 00:04:46.856
Permanent IDs take priority; ambiguous matches
need manual selection.

109
00:04:46.856 --> 00:04:50.681
Here, the cleaning solution's open-use quantity
remains unknown, while its closed-use

110
00:04:50.681 --> 00:04:51.896
quantity is confirmed zero.

111
00:04:51.896 --> 00:04:55.293
Check the review confirmation and apply the
import only after errors are resolved and

112
00:04:55.293 --> 00:04:56.252
warnings are understood.

113
00:04:57.079 --> 00:05:00.266
Check the saved inventory and import history
after applying the workbook.

114
00:05:00.230 --> 00:05:03.615
Rows omitted from a return are retained;
omission does not remove stock.

115
00:05:03.615 --> 00:05:07.330
Mark products No longer used or Duplicate when
appropriate and explain the decision.

116
00:05:07.330 --> 00:05:10.932
The app converts compatible volume units to
gallons and mass units to pounds, without

117
00:05:10.932 --> 00:05:12.543
inferring a mass-to-volume conversion.

118
00:05:12.543 --> 00:05:16.207
Export assessment JSON and Excel, and keep a
dated checkpoint before continuing to

119
00:05:16.207 --> 00:05:17.280
the detailed assessment.

120
00:05:18.147 --> 00:05:21.904
Step five: open the exported Excel workbook and
inspect MAQ Tables.

121
00:05:21.868 --> 00:05:25.512
The current workbook applies automatic
comparisons where classifications match its

122
00:05:25.512 --> 00:05:26.267
supported tables.

123
00:05:26.267 --> 00:05:28.086
YES flags an exceedance for review.

124
00:05:28.086 --> 00:05:31.541
Blank, unresolved, or not-assessed results are
not passing conclusions.

125
00:05:31.541 --> 00:05:34.870
Our sample classifications remain unresolved, so
they cannot demonstrate an

126
00:05:34.870 --> 00:05:36.113
allowable-quantity decision.

127
00:05:36.113 --> 00:05:39.819
Confirm the selected edition, table
applicability, control-area aggregation,

128
00:05:39.819 --> 00:05:42.306
adjustments, and any Group H implications
yourself.

129
00:05:42.306 --> 00:05:46.184
Use Material inventory for unique inventory;
repeated hazard rows are not additional

130
00:05:46.184 --> 00:05:46.461
stock.

131
00:05:47.324 --> 00:05:51.273
Open Assessment and HMIS, then import the
assessment JSON if it is not already

132
00:05:51.273 --> 00:05:51.627
loaded.

133
00:05:51.591 --> 00:05:55.584
Back up any existing record first, because this
import replaces the open assessment.

134
00:05:55.584 --> 00:05:59.330
Review the approved-cabinet setting and project
sprinkler information, including any

135
00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:00.311
per-material override.

136
00:06:00.311 --> 00:06:03.800
Set these only when the actual installation and
applicable criteria support the

137
00:06:03.800 --> 00:06:04.286
adjustment.

138
00:06:04.286 --> 00:06:06.546
Re-export Excel after changing the flags.

139
00:06:06.546 --> 00:06:10.399
A checkbox does not verify the cabinet,
sprinkler coverage, or entitlement to an

140
00:06:10.399 --> 00:06:10.833
increase.

141
00:06:11.695 --> 00:06:15.651
In each hazard record, use Add database
reference to document online corroboration.

142
00:06:15.615 --> 00:06:19.627
The AI instructions require opening
authoritative records such as PubChem, NIOSH, or

143
00:06:19.627 --> 00:06:21.824
CAMEO, rather than relying on search snippets.

144
00:06:21.824 --> 00:06:26.016
Record the specific URL, access date, identity
match, supporting or conflicting

145
00:06:26.016 --> 00:06:27.184
evidence, and finding.

146
00:06:27.184 --> 00:06:31.211
Match CAS number, concentration, form, and
conditions, and explain mixture

147
00:06:31.211 --> 00:06:31.973
applicability.

148
00:06:31.973 --> 00:06:34.077
Our reference is intentionally incomplete.

149
00:06:34.077 --> 00:06:37.537
Resolve outstanding material information and
review the evidence before selecting

150
00:06:37.537 --> 00:06:38.519
Validate this material.

151
00:06:39.368 --> 00:06:41.462
Step six: prepare the room register.

152
00:06:41.426 --> 00:06:44.639
Check Inventory assignment and confirm each line
belongs to the correct room.

153
00:06:44.639 --> 00:06:47.825
Imported locations may already create room
entries, as shown here.

154
00:06:47.825 --> 00:06:51.525
Add room when needed, then enter room number,
name, control-area grouping, and

155
00:06:51.525 --> 00:06:52.900
intended Revit sheet or view.

156
00:06:52.900 --> 00:06:55.023
Keep the same room record when renaming it.

157
00:06:55.023 --> 00:06:58.994
Split actual stock between locations; never copy
a whole-site quantity into every

158
00:06:58.994 --> 00:06:59.239
room.

159
00:06:59.239 --> 00:07:01.187
Verify assignments against the plans.

160
00:07:02.043 --> 00:07:04.874
Review the generated inventory block and
complete the room notes.

161
00:07:04.838 --> 00:07:09.189
The detailed guide calls for scope, hazards,
occupancy and MAQ assessment, containers

162
00:07:09.189 --> 00:07:13.437
and transfer, incompatibilities, containment,
ventilation, signage, fire protection

163
00:07:13.437 --> 00:07:14.614
and alarms, and egress.

164
00:07:14.614 --> 00:07:16.519
Explain not-applicable decisions.

165
00:07:16.519 --> 00:07:20.494
Add source revisions, pages, adopted criteria,
and calculation references.

166
00:07:20.494 --> 00:07:23.933
Finish the content, resolve material questions,
then confirm the room, shared

167
00:07:23.933 --> 00:07:26.747
control-area, and building review before
validating every room.

168
00:07:26.747 --> 00:07:29.682
This training draft remains incomplete and is
not ready for issue.

169
00:07:30.546 --> 00:07:33.255
Use Export draft Revit text during coordination.

170
00:07:33.219 --> 00:07:36.816
Use Export reviewed Revit text only after every
current room is complete and

171
00:07:36.816 --> 00:07:37.289
validated.

172
00:07:37.289 --> 00:07:40.919
Here, the app blocks reviewed export and tells
us to validate the notes and resolve

173
00:07:40.919 --> 00:07:41.706
outstanding items.

174
00:07:41.706 --> 00:07:44.572
That is the correct outcome for this unresolved
training example.

175
00:07:44.572 --> 00:07:46.962
Read the blockers and fix the underlying
records.

176
00:07:46.962 --> 00:07:50.390
Do not use a reviewed filename or a reviewer
name as a substitute for completed

177
00:07:50.390 --> 00:07:51.215
engineering review.

178
00:07:52.063 --> 00:07:54.686
The Revit handoff is a text file for human
placement.

179
00:07:54.650 --> 00:07:58.634
Open it, identify the correct room and stable
ID, and copy the appropriate inventory

180
00:07:58.634 --> 00:07:59.915
and note blocks into Revit.

181
00:07:59.915 --> 00:08:02.678
Choose the view, sheet, text type, and
placement.

182
00:08:02.678 --> 00:08:05.492
Check wrapping, clipping, symbols, and
references.

183
00:08:05.492 --> 00:08:09.493
Reconcile the quantities and units with Excel
and the current JSON, then verify the

184
00:08:09.493 --> 00:08:10.506
exported drawing PDF.

185
00:08:10.506 --> 00:08:13.658
The app does not update the model or confirm
that issued drawings changed.

186
00:08:14.514 --> 00:08:18.384
When the owner changes a quantity, first archive
the current JSON and issued package.

187
00:08:18.348 --> 00:08:21.864
Find the affected inventory line and choose
Record quantities or late change.

188
00:08:21.864 --> 00:08:24.522
Here, storage changes from ten to fifteen
gallons.

189
00:08:24.522 --> 00:08:28.056
Review every quantity field and the unit, then
enter the reason and source notice

190
00:08:28.056 --> 00:08:29.190
with its revision or date.

191
00:08:29.190 --> 00:08:30.706
Save the quantity record.

192
00:08:30.706 --> 00:08:34.195
In this dialog, a unit change is a revision, not
an automatic conversion.

193
00:08:35.063 --> 00:08:38.275
Inspect Quantity change history and verify the
old and new values.

194
00:08:38.239 --> 00:08:41.382
The app keeps a preceding assessment snapshot
and preserves the narrative.

195
00:08:41.382 --> 00:08:45.137
Inventory changes require re-review of all room
notes, including shared control-area

196
00:08:45.137 --> 00:08:46.076
and building effects.

197
00:08:46.076 --> 00:08:50.151
Reassess affected limits, safeguards, and
occupancy conclusions, validate the changed

198
00:08:50.151 --> 00:08:53.843
material and current rooms, then export fresh
JSON, Excel, and reviewed text.

199
00:08:53.843 --> 00:08:57.839
Update all affected Revit notes and callouts,
archive superseded output, and check

200
00:08:57.839 --> 00:08:58.814
the new drawing PDF.

201
00:08:59.676 --> 00:09:01.468
Back up after each major stage.

202
00:09:01.432 --> 00:09:05.879
Complete backup includes original PDFs and
extracted text; workspace JSON alone does

203
00:09:05.879 --> 00:09:06.091
not.

204
00:09:06.091 --> 00:09:09.493
The complete backup supports up to five hundred
megabytes of stored PDFs.

205
00:09:09.493 --> 00:09:13.608
For larger projects, retain the original
packages, workspace JSON, and AI batches

206
00:09:13.608 --> 00:09:14.065
together.

207
00:09:14.065 --> 00:09:16.751
Browser storage is local to that browser and
device.

208
00:09:16.751 --> 00:09:20.281
Keep the latest Assessment and HMIS JSON after
room edits or late changes; returning

209
00:09:20.281 --> 00:09:23.055
to an older bulk export does not carry those
newer edits backward.

210
00:09:23.890 --> 00:09:27.705
Finish by reconciling every delivered file and
page, confirmed product, analysis

211
00:09:27.705 --> 00:09:30.280
result or open question, and owner inventory
location.

212
00:09:30.244 --> 00:09:33.865
Confirm the engineering conclusions and
outstanding actions, and retain the sources

213
00:09:33.865 --> 00:09:34.956
with the current exports.

214
00:09:34.956 --> 00:09:38.538
Use Simple instructions for the sequence,
Detailed bulk guide for intake and

215
00:09:38.538 --> 00:09:41.319
recovery, and the HMIS guide for rooms, changes,
and Revit.

216
00:09:41.319 --> 00:09:44.726
That completes the workflow from the owner's
package to a recoverable, reviewed

217
00:09:44.726 --> 00:09:45.415
project handoff.
